  "reason": "The fix addresses the root cause identified in the bug report. The issue was that option descriptions in the help text were exceeding the configured terminal width (80 characters). The problem was in the `write_dl` method in `src/click/formatting.py` at line 242. The `text_width` calculation did not account for `self.current_indent`, causing the wrapped text to be calculated with too much available width. When continuation lines were then indented by `first_col + self.current_indent`, the total line length exceeded the terminal width. By subtracting `self.current_indent` from the `text_width` calculation, wrapped text now respects the full width constraint including indentation. This ensures that option descriptions, like the `--name` option with the repeated 'wordy' text, will wrap correctly and no line will exceed the configured terminal width of 80 characters."
}
```

